The root cause of the hover double-outline or glow issue on small icon-style buttons was identified as a mismatch between the system's default focus outline and the custom focus-shadow applied by the design team. Specifically, the custom focus-shadow was being applied on top of the system's default focus outline, leading to a double outline or glow effect.

To prevent stacked shadow artifacts, Evan suggested a CSS solution that prefers the custom shadow for brand consistency under normal conditions but falls back to the system's default focus outline in high-contrast mode. The proposed CSS is as follows:

```css
.icon-btn:focus { outline: none; box-shadow: var(--focus-shadow); }
@media (forced-colors: active) { .icon-btn:focus { box-shadow: none; outline: 2px solid Highlight; } }
```

This ensures that in high-contrast mode, the system's default focus outline is used, avoiding the double outline or glow issue.
